(r/'README.md').write_text('Fixing required-cut indices, or fixing both cut and occupation indices, does not improve ray coverage at the tested one-domain allocation. All297 queries still need exact-point fallback. Final RHS maps and ordered nonzero conditions are identical to fully anchored rays. Single3 retains64 applicable results and844 RHS terms; double retains31 applicable results,4 explicit NoRule results and307 RHS terms.\n\nThe sample includes every actual initial round000 request plus the seven earlier targeted depth labels:64 single3 and35 double labels after deduplication. Initial and later checkpoint source identities are checked exactly. The historical program is replayed only to validate previous leaf/control selections and record initial statuses, then discarded. Native discovery remains the only reducer; no previous rules or numerical references enter it.\n\nEvery arm uses the same original sources, role admission, zeros, coordinate order, sample seed0, depth3, ray cap1 and exact-point fallback cap1. The only difference is the ray box: all nonzero coordinates anchored; or required cuts fixed; or required cuts and occupations fixed. Ordinary coordinates always retain their anchored symbolic powers. All297 encoded programs independently decode/replay with admitted RHS labels, including the12 programs whose requested point remains explicitly unresolved. Search gaps are retained.\n\nFixed-role rays sometimes add an unused rule, so the applicable point rule can move from ordinal0 to1. Rule totals across independent programs increase64→68 for single3 and31→40/43 for double; this is not a coverage gain. These results do not rule out different domain budgets, but provide no reason to enable fixed-role rays under the tested allocation. Shared-host timings include historical replay and are not a performance comparison.\n\nAll point proof binaries are deterministically gzipped with mtime0 and byte-exact roundtrip verification; archives.json maps their original logical paths and hashes. Input source binaries remain raw. See summary.json for exact counts/conditions comparisons and the per-arm result files for full proof source traces and uncovered domains.\n')
